OL,3,GNEWSA'A lot of military wives give up
OL,4,Atheir dreams'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThey are often described as the "anchor
OL,7,Fof the household" in Army families.
OL,9,FMilitary wives can play the role of
OL,10,Fboth mum and dad and run the show when
OL,11,Fit is time to move again - often at
OL,12,Fgreat cost to their own lives.
OL,14,F"I think a lot of military wives give
OL,15,Fup their dreams, hopes and aspirations
OL,16,Fbecause it's so difficult to organise
OL,17,Fyourself and think 'how am I going to
OL,18,Fnow deal with being a single parent?',"
OL,19,Fsaid Anna Barkway, who has been based
OL,20,Fat Rock Barracks in Suffolk for nine
OL,21,Fyears.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
